  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development of one document including guidelines, standard procedures and training</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Equip MISAU with technical assistance, knowledge, and tools to effectively construct and maintain a sustainable intermediary medical warehouse. Development of one document including guidelines, standard procedures and training.
UNDP&#x2019;s mandate demands capacity development as an integral component of any intervention. Through knowledge sharing, local personnel can take greater ownership of maintaining functioning warehouses for improved storage and distribution capacities.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Construction of a newly HQ for CMAM in Zimpeto, Maputo province</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved management of medicines, vaccines, and other health product distribution and storage operations at National level: Zimpeto, HQ. Construction of a newly HQ for CMAM in Zimpeto, Maputo province. 
It is important to enhance management operations for medicine and vaccine distribution, optimizing logistics, bolstering quality assurance, and ensuring timely oversight. Streamlining processes increase the reach to rights-holders while enhancing surveillance of distribution and storage capacities. This synergy maximizes efficiency, ensuring prompt delivery and maintaining the integrity of life-saving supplies.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Construction of a newly  Intermediary Medical Warehouse, Nampula province, including Environmental Licensing</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved safety, security and storage conditions of medicines, vaccines, and other health products at sub-national level: Nampula. Construction of a newly Intermediary Medical Warehouse, Nampula province, including Environmental Licensing.
It is important to decentralize storage and distribution capacities for drugs and consumables, so as reduce pressures on urban centers, reach people in rural areas, and expand access to care. This warehouse will have a storage capacity of 750 euro pallets.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of Medical Warehouses equipped (forklift, shelves)</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Warehouse equipped with shelves for the accurate and safety storage of goods and handling equipment for the operation of the reception and dispatch of orders as well as internal movement.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
